VYNT Technologies — Explanation of Products and Scopes

VYNT Technologies is an AI-powered gaming intelligence platform designed to help gaming creators analyze, optimize, manage, and improve their social media content. VYNT provides a centralized dashboard where creators can connect authorized social media accounts and use platform data for content analytics, AI-powered recommendations, content optimization, forecasting, and publishing workflows.

VYNT uses TikTok’s official developer products and OAuth authorization to allow creators to securely connect their TikTok accounts. VYNT does not request a creator’s TikTok password and does not use browser automation, credential sharing, scraping, or methods intended to bypass TikTok’s platform controls.

When a creator chooses to connect TikTok to VYNT, the creator is redirected through TikTok’s official authorization flow. The creator signs into TikTok and reviews the permissions requested by VYNT. Only after the creator provides authorization does VYNT receive the applicable authorization credentials and access authorized TikTok information.

1. Login Kit

VYNT uses TikTok Login Kit to provide secure account authentication and account connection.

The VYNT website includes a “Connect TikTok” workflow. When a creator selects this option, VYNT initiates TikTok’s OAuth authorization process. The creator is redirected to TikTok where they authenticate and authorize the requested permissions.

After successful authorization, TikTok provides an authorization code to VYNT’s authorized callback endpoint. VYNT’s backend exchanges this code for the appropriate access credentials and securely associates the authorized TikTok account with the creator’s VYNT account.

Login Kit is primarily used to establish the relationship between a VYNT user and their authorized TikTok account. VYNT does not use Login Kit to obtain a user’s TikTok password or authentication credentials directly.

The connected account is displayed inside VYNT so the creator can confirm which TikTok account is currently connected.

If a creator disconnects TikTok from VYNT or revokes authorization, VYNT will no longer use the revoked authorization to access TikTok resources.

2. Display API

VYNT uses TikTok’s Display API to retrieve information from a creator’s authorized TikTok account for display and analytics functionality.

The Display API allows VYNT to obtain authorized profile and video information and present that information inside the VYNT dashboard.

For example, after connecting TikTok, a creator may see their TikTok profile information and authorized videos within VYNT’s Content or Analytics sections. This allows the creator to work with their TikTok content without having to manually enter each video’s information into VYNT.

VYNT uses the retrieved video information as an input for its content intelligence system. Depending on the information made available through the approved TikTok products and scopes, VYNT can organize content records and associate them with analytics, keywords, topics, and AI-generated recommendations.

VYNT’s purpose is not to reproduce TikTok as a separate social network. Instead, TikTok information is used as an authorized data source for the creator’s VYNT dashboard and content intelligence workflow.

3. Content Posting API

VYNT uses TikTok’s Content Posting API to support creator-authorized publishing workflows.

VYNT is designed to allow a creator to prepare gaming content within the VYNT platform and use TikTok’s official publishing functionality to publish that content to the creator’s TikTok account.

For example, a creator may prepare a gaming video and use VYNT’s Content Lab to work on the video’s caption, keywords, hashtags, and other metadata. VYNT can then provide the creator with a publishing workflow through the authorized TikTok integration.

Publishing is performed through TikTok’s official API functionality rather than through browser automation or simulated user actions.

VYNT’s automation system is designed around creator authorization and configurable automation modes. Depending on the creator’s settings and the capabilities approved by TikTok, the creator may review and approve content before publishing.

VYNT does not intentionally publish unrelated or unauthorized content to a creator’s account.

4. Scope: user.info.basic

VYNT uses the user.info.basic scope to identify and display basic information about the TikTok account that the creator has authorized.

This information is used to associate the TikTok account with the correct VYNT user and to provide account context within the dashboard.

For example, VYNT may display the creator’s TikTok display name, profile information, avatar, or TikTok account identifier where permitted by the approved API response.

This information helps prevent confusion when a creator has multiple connected social accounts.

The information is not used to access the creator’s TikTok password or private authentication credentials.

5. Scope: video.list

VYNT uses the video.list scope to retrieve the authorized creator’s TikTok video information through TikTok’s official API.

The purpose of this scope is to allow VYNT to identify and display the creator’s authorized TikTok videos inside the VYNT dashboard.

Retrieved video information can be associated with VYNT’s content intelligence system. VYNT can organize videos by creator, content type, gaming topic, keyword, and other available metadata.

The video information may also be used by VYNT’s analytics and AI systems to provide creator-focused insights.

For example, VYNT may use authorized video information as part of workflows that help a creator understand which types of gaming content they have published, organize their content library, identify recurring topics, and generate optimization suggestions.

VYNT’s AI features are intended to assist the creator rather than impersonate TikTok’s own recommendation system. VYNT does not claim that its proprietary scores or recommendations represent TikTok’s actual ranking algorithm.

6. AI Analysis and Content Intelligence

TikTok data authorized by the creator can be processed by VYNT’s content intelligence system.

VYNT may analyze available content information to generate structured insights such as gaming topics, keywords, content categories, search-oriented recommendations, and optimization suggestions.

The creator may use these insights through VYNT’s Intelligence, SEO, Analytics, Forecast, Content Lab, Copilot, and Autopilot features.

For example, a creator could connect their TikTok account, import authorized video information, and use VYNT to organize their gaming content and receive recommendations for future content.

AI-generated information is presented as assistance and analysis. VYNT does not represent AI-generated recommendations as official TikTok recommendations, rankings, or guarantees of future performance.

7. Data Storage and Security

VYNT handles TikTok authorization information through its backend rather than intentionally exposing sensitive credentials in the public frontend.

OAuth credentials and other sensitive configuration values are intended to be stored using server-side environment variables and secure backend storage.

VYNT does not intentionally place TikTok client secrets, access tokens, API keys, database credentials, or other sensitive secrets in its public GitHub repository.

The public VYNT GitHub repository is intended primarily for product documentation, public information, legal documents, examples, and project materials rather than private production credentials or proprietary backend source code.

8. Creator Control

VYNT is designed around creator authorization and control.

Creators decide whether to connect their TikTok account to VYNT. The creator is presented with TikTok’s authorization process before VYNT receives access to the approved resources.

Creators can disconnect their TikTok account from VYNT. Where applicable, creators can also revoke VYNT’s authorization through TikTok.

VYNT does not require creators to provide their TikTok password directly to VYNT.

9. Purpose of the Integration

The purpose of the TikTok integration is to provide gaming creators with a centralized platform for managing and analyzing their authorized TikTok content.

The integration allows VYNT to connect TikTok account information and authorized video information with VYNT’s broader gaming intelligence platform.

VYNT’s goal is to reduce the amount of manual work required to organize gaming content, understand content performance, develop content strategies, and manage publishing workflows.

The TikTok integration is therefore a core component of VYNT’s creator workflow, while TikTok remains the platform where the creator’s TikTok account and published content reside.

10. Use of Official TikTok APIs

VYNT intends to use TikTok’s official developer products and approved API capabilities for its TikTok integration.

VYNT does not intentionally use unauthorized scraping, automated browser control, credential sharing, or other methods designed to circumvent TikTok’s authentication or platform restrictions.

VYNT only requests the TikTok products and scopes necessary for the functionality being implemented and will follow the applicable requirements associated with those products and scopes.

The exact information available to VYNT is limited by the products, scopes, permissions, and API capabilities approved by TikTok.

VYNT will not represent an unavailable TikTok API capability as available functionality.

11. Summary

In summary, VYNT uses TikTok Login Kit to allow creators to securely authenticate and connect their TikTok accounts. VYNT uses the Display API and applicable authorized scopes to retrieve permitted profile and video information for display and content intelligence. VYNT uses the Content Posting API to support creator-authorized publishing workflows.

The user.info.basic scope is used to identify and display basic information about the authorized TikTok account, while the video.list scope is used to retrieve authorized TikTok video information for the creator’s VYNT dashboard and analytics workflows.

The information obtained through these integrations is used to provide VYNT’s gaming intelligence features, including content organization, analytics, AI-assisted insights, keyword and topic analysis, optimization recommendations, and content management.

VYNT is designed to give creators control over their connected accounts and to use TikTok’s official authorization and API mechanisms rather than requesting passwords or using unauthorized access methods.